{
  "description": "Shared shell-command risk policy (GOVERNANCE.md \u00a720.3), loaded by packages/execution-adapters (Go, embedded) and scos_execution (Python); both implement the same algorithm and are checked against risk_cases.json. A command is split on unquoted ; | & && || newlines, command substitution and subshells; leading VAR=value assignments and the launchers below are unwrapped (a shell's -c script is classified in turn); the program is the basename of the first word, compared in lower case (flags keep their case). Each segment is graded by its program, and the command takes its most dangerous segment. Only programs listed as read (with read subcommands where listed) are read: any program not named here is write, so an unrecognised command always needs governance. Output redirection to a file is at least write, to a block device destructive.",
  "version": 2,
  "max_depth": 6,
